dsv41 patch 0074b (24.10.2026, applies after 0084): larger background prefill chunks while no foreground request is present.
Why: 0074 keeps background chunks (priority >= VLLM_PREFILL_THROTTLE_MIN_PRIO) at long_prefill_token_threshold even
when the background request is alone, so a foreground request that arrives only waits for a short chunk. With 8 slots
(threshold 512) a lone 950K background prefill takes 770 s instead of 440 s.
How: while no foreground request runs, waits, or sits in kv_holding_waiting, the per-request cap becomes
max(threshold, min(VLLM_DSV41_BG_IDLE_TOKENS, input budget) // eligible requests). Also extends 0073: a foreground
request in kv_holding_waiting (reloading its prefix from the KV offload) now counts as waiting.
Switches: VLLM_DSV41_BG_IDLE_TOKENS (0 = off), VLLM_DSV41_BG_IDLE_FILE (file, read at most every 2 s, overrides live).
